From: Seeed Rockchip BSP
Subject: [PATCH] media: rockchip: isp: report MIN_BUFFERS_FOR_CAPTURE

The RK3588 ISP30 capture queue drops every third frame when only two
buffers are queued by userspace (~9.5fps instead of the mode 0 nominal
14.35fps at 4608x2592 input; reproducible with a bare V4L2 polling
loop).  Three queued buffers sustain the full frame rate.  The ISP39
(RK3576) does not have this limitation.

GStreamer v4l2src sizes its pool from
V4L2_CID_MIN_BUFFERS_FOR_CAPTURE; since the driver did not implement
the control, the pool defaulted to two buffers and every GStreamer
capture pipeline ran at ~9.5fps on this platform.

Implement the control (read-only, default 3) on the rkisp ctrl
handler and attach it to the capture video nodes, so that userspace
pools are sized correctly.  No effect on ISP39, which already
sustains the full frame rate with two buffers.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/isp/capture.c b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/isp/capture.c
index e7872d308fca2..1bae4b12e308e 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/isp/capture.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/isp/capture.c
@@ -1879,6 +1879,7 @@ int rkisp_register_stream_vdev(struct rkisp_stream *stream)
 	vdev->lock = &stream->apilock;
 	vdev->device_caps = V4L2_CAP_VIDEO_CAPTURE_MPLANE |
 				V4L2_CAP_STREAMING;
+	vdev->ctrl_handler = &dev->ctrl_handler;
 	video_set_drvdata(vdev, stream);
 	vdev->vfl_dir = VFL_DIR_RX;
 	node->pad.flags = MEDIA_PAD_FL_SINK;
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/isp/dev.c b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/isp/dev.c
index 6f19ace1b033a..95bc40ef0b49e 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/isp/dev.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/isp/dev.c
@@ -989,8 +989,18 @@ static int rkisp_plat_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	v4l2_dev = &isp_dev->v4l2_dev;
 	v4l2_dev->mdev = &isp_dev->media_dev;
 	strscpy(v4l2_dev->name, isp_dev->name, sizeof(v4l2_dev->name));
-	v4l2_ctrl_handler_init(&isp_dev->ctrl_handler, 5);
+	v4l2_ctrl_handler_init(&isp_dev->ctrl_handler, 6);
 	v4l2_dev->ctrl_handler = &isp_dev->ctrl_handler;
+	/*
+	 * Report the minimum capture buffer count so userspace (GStreamer
+	 * v4l2src) sizes its pool correctly. The ISP30 drops every third
+	 * frame when only two buffers are queued (~9.5fps at 4608x2592
+	 * input); three queued buffers sustain the full frame rate.
+	 */
+	v4l2_ctrl_new_std(&isp_dev->ctrl_handler, NULL,
+			  V4L2_CID_MIN_BUFFERS_FOR_CAPTURE,
+			  1, VIDEO_MAX_FRAME, 1, 3);
+	v4l2_info(v4l2_dev, "rkisp: MIN_BUFFERS_FOR_CAPTURE=3 registered");
 
 	ret = v4l2_device_register(isp_dev->dev, &isp_dev->v4l2_dev);
 	if (ret < 0) {
